data.reasoningText:
Good, I have the project structure. It's a Blazor Web App with Interactive Server render mode, using Bootstrap. Let me plan the component decomposition and then implement.

## Component Plan: Product Catalog

### Component Tree
```
Catalog                    (page — owns filter/sort/page state, orchestrates layout)
├── CatalogSidebar         (filter controls: categories, price, stock)
├── CatalogToolbar         (sort dropdown, showing X-Y of Z label)
├── ProductGrid            (grid of product cards)
│   └── ProductCard        (individual product card)
└── CatalogPagination      (prev/next/numbered page buttons)
```

Now I'm mapping out the data flow: the Catalog component will manage all the state for filtering, sorting, and pagination, then pass relevant data down to each child component. The sidebar, toolbar, and pagination components will emit events back up when the user makes changes, while the product grid displays the filtered results and handles product interactions like selection and adding to cart.

For implementation, I'll build from the bottom up starting with ProductCard as the leaf component, then compose it into ProductGrid, followed by the three sidebar components, and finally wire everything together in the main Catalog page. Since I'm familiar with Blazor patterns, I'll implement these directly rather than using a skill, creating them in a Components/Pages/Catalog/ subfolder to keep the page-specific components organized.

```

csharp
// Components/Pages/Catalog/ProductCard.razor
@if (Product != null)
{
    <div class="product-card">
        <img src="@Product.ImageUrl" alt="@Product.Name" />
        <h3>@Product.Name</h3>
        <p class="price">$@Product.Price.ToString("F2")</p>
        <button @onclick="() => OnAddToCart.InvokeAsync(Product)">Add to Cart</button>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public Product Product { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Product> OnAddToCart { get; set; }
}
```

```csharp
// Components/Pages/Catalog/ProductGrid.razor
<div class="product-grid">
    @foreach (var product in Products)
    {
        <ProductCard Product="product" OnAddToCart="OnAddToCart" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public List<Product> Products { get; set; } = new();

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Product> OnAddToCart { get; set; }
}
```

```csharp
// Components/Pages/Catalog/CatalogSidebar.razor
<aside class="catalog-sidebar">
    <div class="filter-section">
        <h3>Filters</h3>
        <label>
            <input type="checkbox" @bind="SelectedCategories" value="electronics" />
            Electronics
        </label>
        <label>
            <input type="checkbox" @bind="SelectedCategories" value="clothing" />
            Clothing
        </label>
    </div>
    <div class="price-range">
        <label>Max Price: $@MaxPrice</label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="1000" @bind="MaxPrice" />
    </div>
    <button @onclick="ApplyFilters" class="btn-primary">Apply Filters</button>
</aside>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<FilterOptions> OnFiltersChanged { get; set; }

    private List<string> SelectedCategories = new();
    private decimal MaxPrice = 1000;

    private async Task ApplyFilters()
    {
        var filters = new FilterOptions 
        { 
            Categories = SelectedCategories, 
            MaxPrice = MaxPrice 
        };
        await OnFiltersChanged.InvokeAsync(filters);
    }
}
```

